# Pick ONE way to reach a language model. Without any of these, `cosorag ask --no-llm` still works (retrieval + citations).

# Option A: AWS Bedrock (what the reported results used). gpt-oss-120b is open-weight (Apache 2.0), served in Mumbai.
AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=
COSORAG_LLM=bedrock:openai.gpt-oss-120b-1:0
# COSORAG_LLM_REGION=ap-south-1

# Option B: any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (Ollama, vLLM, Groq, OpenRouter, Gemini's OpenAI endpoint ...)
# COSORAG_LLM=openai:qwen2.5:7b-instruct
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=ollama

# Optional overrides
# COSORAG_RERANKER=none            # disable the fine-tuned reranker / grounding gate
# COSORAG_EMBEDDER=intfloat/multilingual-e5-small
